{
  "$comment": "Round 1 review (renderer hardening): interaction semantics every renderer must share, HAND-AUTHORED and replayed by packages/exponential-ui-react/src/interactions-fixture.test.tsx (the reference, jsdom) and apps/desktop/crates/exponential-ui/tests/interactions_fixture.rs (the core, so gpui and the natives through the FFI). numberField: a NumberField bound to /v (value null = /v unseeded), one op (increment / decrement press, commit = type `input` then leave the field, none), then the value at /v and the text the field shows (en-US; `precision` absent = the step's decimals; values round like toFixed, the text like Intl.NumberFormat with that many fraction digits; a stepper on an unset value starts from min when min > 0, else 0; a stepper at its limit is disabled). checks: a Form `f` holding Checkbox `agree` (checked bound to /agreed) with `checks` and a submit Button; submitting gives the failing messages in order (a check WITH a condition fails when it resolves to nothing, null, false or an empty string; 0 passes; a non-string message reads `Invalid value`) and whether `submit` fired. tableSort: an UNBOUND sort of literal rows by one column (`sortRows`: missing values last both ways, two numbers numerically, a number column coerces, a date column by time, booleans as 0/1, the rest by Intl.Collator(locale, {numeric: true, sensitivity: base}); ties keep row order) → the row indexes in display order. choiceTiles (EXP-1280): a ChoiceTiles `c` over options a, b, c (`disabled` = the index of a disabled option) with `value` bound to /v (null = unseeded), the tiles pressed in order (a press on any part of tile i), then /v and every `change` value fired: single picks the pressed value; multiple toggles it in the comma-joined list kept in OPTION order (nothing picked = an empty string); a disabled option does nothing. select (VAPP-146): a plain single Select `s` over the options Any (value \"\"), Open (open) and Done (done) with `value` bound to /v (null = unseeded), the options picked in order (open the trigger, press option i), then /v, the text the trigger shows and every `change` value fired: an empty string is an ordinary option value (never refused, never the error placeholder); an unseeded value reads as \"\", so the trigger shows the option holding \"\"; picking an option writes its value; picking the option that holds the current value fires nothing (the empty one included, an unseeded /v stays unseeded). buttonHold (VAPP-162, docs/round-5-contract.md §9): a Button `b` (label `Hold to talk`, `holdingLabel` `Holding…` unless the case says otherwise) laid out at 120 × 40 px, coordinates relative to its top-left; `props` override the button's (null = unset; the base props are `hold: true`); `steps` = pointerdown/pointermove/pointerup at {x, y}, pointercancel, keydown/keyup {key}, blur; after each step `events` = the events that step fired (in order) and `pressed` / `label` = what the button paints. THE RULE: with `hold: true` a press never fires `press`; pointer down (or Space/Enter key down; key repeat ignored) fires `holdStart` and paints the pressed state + `holdingLabel`; while the hold is active the pointer may wander up to 24 px (the slop) outside the box; release (pointer up anywhere within the slop, or key up of the key that started it) fires `holdEnd`; the pointer leaving the box by more than the slop (the slide away), pointercancel, Escape or losing focus fire `holdCancel`; after a cancel nothing fires until the next down. `disabled` fires nothing; `hold: false` keeps the plain `press` on release over the box.",
